# Flutter architecture

Layout per feature: `lib/features/<feature>/{domain,data,presentation}` — see `CLAUDE.md` for the full tree.

- `domain/` is pure Dart: no `package:flutter`, `cloud_firestore`, `firebase_*` or `get_it` imports.
- Entities: `class <Name>Entity extends Equatable`, `const` constructor, all fields `final`, `props` lists every field.
- Models: `class <Name>Model extends <Name>Entity` with `factory fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json, {String? documentId})` and `toJson()`. Timestamps via `FirebaseDTConverter`.
- Data source interface: `data/data_source/<name>_service.dart` → `abstract class <Name>DataSource`. Implementation: `data/data_source/remote/<name>_service.dart` → `<Name>DataSourceImpl`.
- Return `Future<DataState<T>>` (`DataSuccess` / `DataError(error: AppError(error:, code:, message:))`) from data sources and repositories. Catch exceptions in the data source, `log(...)` them with the stack trace (`dart:developer`), and return `AppError(error: e, code: '500')`; use `code: '404'` for missing docs and `'400'` for bad input.
- Use cases: one class per action, `extends UseCase<R, P>`, `call({required P param})`; params in `usecases/utils/<name>_param.dart`.
- Inject `FirebaseFirestore` / `FirebaseFunctions` / `FirebaseAuth` through constructors; only `lib/di.dart` uses `.instance`. Collection names from `FirebaseCollections`.
- Register in `lib/di.dart` inside `_initialize<Feature>()`; call it from `initializeDependency`.
- No `print` in new code; use `log` from `dart:developer`.
